WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.737 align:start size:78% position:22% line:0%
- Hello, I'm Gav.
- I'm Dan.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.440 align:start position:0% line:0%
Welcome to the first episode
of "Planet Slow Mo."

00:00:07.473 --> 00:00:09.675 align:start size:78% position:22% line:0%
For the next 12 weeks,
we're gonna be travelling
around the world

00:00:09.708 --> 00:00:11.377 align:start size:63% position:38%
to all kinds
of exotic locations.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.379 align:start position:0%
We've separated each episode
into two parts.

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:15.648 align:start position:0%
In part one,
we'll travel somewhere
we've never been before,

00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:18.084 align:start position:0%
film something
pretty wicked in slow-mo.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:21.054 align:start position:0%
And in part two,
we'll take a deeper dive into
the science of what we've shot

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:23.056 size:75% position:38%
and analyze our footage.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.558 align:start size:69% position:31%
For the first episode,
I thought we'd go
somewhere cool.

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:27.394 align:start position:0%
I like it,
I like what you've done there.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.804
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.473 align:start position:0%
Today we're on a glacier
in Iceland.

00:00:40.506 --> 00:00:41.841 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Where's that?
- That's in Iceland.

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:43.376 align:start size:81% position:19%
- That makes sense.
- Makes sense.

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:44.844 align:start size:69% position:31%
Yeah. So wait,
if we're on a glacier,

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:46.846 align:start size:88% position:13%
does that mean we're already
moving in super slow-mo?

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:48.748 align:start position:0%
Yeah, this is literally
the perfect place for us.

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:50.383 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Yeah.
- We're gonna travel
  around Iceland

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:52.285 align:start position:0%
and film some of
its natural beauties

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:55.655 align:start position:0%
in some lovely 4K 1,000
frames a second slow-motion.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.223 size:75% position:38%
And it should look lush.

00:00:57.256 --> 00:00:58.491 align:start size:59% position:41%
Mm. Should we start
with the geyser?

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:00.160 align:start position:0%
Start with the--
which way is that?

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:03.262 align:start size:72% position:28%
Actually, I don't know.

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:05.531 align:start size:59% position:41%
There's not really
any identifiable...

00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:07.233 align:start position:0%
Should we just head in a
direction and hope for the best?

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:08.267 align:start position:0%
Yeah, let's go
to the white.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.502 align:start size:50% position:50%
All right, yeah.

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:16.175
- ( grunts )
- ( laughs )

00:01:16.208 --> 00:01:17.510 align:start size:47% position:53%
Oh, you Muppet.

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:20.146
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:32.692 align:start size:63% position:38% line:0%
This is
the Strokkur Geyser.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.160 align:start position:0%
You nailed
that Icelandic.

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:35.394 align:start size:66% position:34%
Thank you.
Or if you're English,

00:01:35.427 --> 00:01:38.264 align:start size:84% position:16%
- the Strokkur Geyser.
- Man: Whoo!

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:41.234 align:start position:0%
Or if you're American,
"Guy-zer."

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Whatever, right?
- Is that right, "guy-zer"?

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:43.669 align:start size:16% position:84%
Yeah.

00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:44.837 align:start size:81% position:19%
- We're all correct.
- Yeah.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.739 align:start position:0%
It goes off every
five to ten minutes.

00:01:46.772 --> 00:01:48.508 align:start position:0%
And we've seen it hit
40 meters in the air.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.510 align:start size:88% position:13%
- It's gone really high.
- Really high.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.512 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Yeah.
- So we're gonna whip out
  the Phantom Flex 4K

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:55.615 align:start position:0%
and get some lovely
1,000-frames-a-second shots

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.750 align:start position:0%
of it going off.

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.318 align:start position:0%
Smells a bit like eggs.

00:01:59.351 --> 00:02:00.453 align:start size:66% position:34%
Sorry,
that was me that one.

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:01.754 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Oh, was that you?
- Yeah.

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:05.458
Gav: All right, here we are.

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:07.426
Filming in the rain,
bit of a mare.

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:09.162
Uh, why won't-- oh!

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:11.430 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Oh!
- That was a good one.

00:02:11.463 --> 00:02:12.798
That was a bloody good one.

00:02:12.831 --> 00:02:15.435
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:02:20.472 --> 00:02:21.874
Dan:<i> Oh, that's big there,
 look at that!</i>

00:02:21.907 --> 00:02:23.309
Gav:<i> That is massive.</i>

00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:24.744
Dan:<i> That's huge.</i>

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.579
<i> It's almost coming out
 the side.</i>

00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:29.883 align:start position:0%
<i>Came out at like four different
places at once there.</i>

00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:35.188
Gav:
<i> Got some height on that one.</i>

00:02:38.824 --> 00:02:40.927
Wow, that was a great one.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.495 align:start size:34% position:66%
How wicked.

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:44.564
- That was wicked.
- That was perfect.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:47.300 align:start size:78% position:22%
That particular one there
was a really bubbly one.

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.734 align:start size:84% position:16%
That might be the bubbliest
one that I've seen.

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:50.469 align:start size:47% position:53%
It sort of like
slowly does it

00:02:50.502 --> 00:02:52.305 align:start size:63% position:38%
and then
eventually explodes.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:53.906 align:start size:53% position:47%
Sometimes it just
goes straight up.

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:55.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Should we watch that back?
- Yeah.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.643
Gav:<i> All right, playing back.</i>

00:03:00.312 --> 00:03:01.781 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Ooh!
- Okay, look at that.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.616 align:start position:0%
- God.
- It's really blue under there.

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:04.817 align:start size:69% position:31%
It looks like a giant,
it's just explosion

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.586 align:start size:78% position:22%
underneath all the water.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:07.887 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then it finally--
see where it breaks the tension

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.989 align:start size:84% position:16%
- of the water there?
- Yeah.

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:12.725 align:start size:81% position:19%
- That was cool.
- Gav:<i> It's wherever
 the gas comes out</i>

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:14.860
<i> of the bubble first,
 that's where it rushes out</i>

00:03:14.893 --> 00:03:16.495
<i> and then it immediately
 drains the bubble.</i>

00:03:16.528 --> 00:03:17.730
Dan:<i> Yeah, the bubble
 just gets drained.</i>

00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:19.665
Seems like
it's completely random.

00:03:19.698 --> 00:03:21.567 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Totally random.
- It's just based on
  what bubble comes up.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.002 align:start size:16% position:84%
Yeah.

00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:24.904
( people clamoring )

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:33.646
Gav:<i> I want to be really tight
 on that bub.</i>

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:35.448
Dan:<i> And that bub was good.</i>

00:03:40.552 --> 00:03:41.954
<i> Where's it break?
 Oh, there it goes</i>

00:03:41.987 --> 00:03:43.923 align:start size:78% position:22%
- Dan:<i> ( hisses ) </i>
-<i> ( chuckles )</i>

00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:46.326
Dan:<i> It's quite a bit of,
like, surface tension it seems.</i>

00:03:49.561 --> 00:03:51.564
<i> Really gets quite big
 before it explodes</i>

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:53.333
<i> and then it just loses it.</i>

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:58.504 align:start position:0%
I feel like it'd be
really good if we got...

00:03:58.537 --> 00:03:59.872 align:start position:0%
the top down,
like looking...

00:03:59.905 --> 00:04:01.307 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Ah, I'll stop you there.
- Yeah?

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.908 align:start size:81% position:19%
- I got it covered.
- All right.

00:04:02.941 --> 00:04:05.311 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
- I've been working
  on something.
- Okay.

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:08.347 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
- Right then.
- Phantom with a drone.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.049 size:84% position:42% line:0%
Right, so by working on it,

00:04:10.082 --> 00:04:13.653 align:start position:0% line:0%
you mean you've tied your drone
to the Phantom with string.

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.655 line:0%
- Yeah.
- Okay.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:17.890 align:start position:0% line:0%
Are you concerned with
the weight of the Phantom

00:04:17.923 --> 00:04:20.593 size:88% position:44% line:0%
and the fact that it's got
a massive, heavy lens on it?

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:21.894 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
- No.
- No, it'll be fine, right?

00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:23.462 align:start position:0% line:0%
- Yeah.
- All right, let's give it a go.

00:04:23.495 --> 00:04:24.597 align:start size:53% position:47%
Okay, here we go.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.032 align:start position:0%
This is typically
a no-drone area,

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:27.600
but we have got
special permission.

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:28.835 align:start size:34% position:66%
Stand back.

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.806 align:start size:31% position:69%
( grunts )
Come on!

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:35.408 align:start size:66% position:34%
- Come on!
- Dan.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:36.643 size:78% position:39%
Dan, I'll stop you there.

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:42.882
I'll stop you there.

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.550
I've got something
different in mind.

00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:46.085 align:start size:31% position:69%
All right.

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:47.386
Why don't you look up?

00:04:47.419 --> 00:04:49.822
<i> ( fanfare )</i>

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.735 align:start size:72% position:28% line:0%
- Well, hello.
- Hello.

00:05:02.768 --> 00:05:04.804 align:start position:0% line:0%
This is the biggest drone
I've ever seen.

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:06.872 align:start position:0% line:0%
You want to
tell us about it?

00:05:06.905 --> 00:05:10.042 align:start size:91% position:9%
It is probably one of the
largest commercial drones
in the world

00:05:10.075 --> 00:05:11.944
for aerial photography.

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:14.513 align:start position:0%
Of all the Phantoms
we've ever used,

00:05:14.546 --> 00:05:15.614 size:75% position:38%
this is the biggest one.

00:05:15.647 --> 00:05:17.049 align:start size:81% position:19%
The biggest Phantom? Yeah.

00:05:17.082 --> 00:05:18.684
Dan: We've also got
a bunch of other stuff

00:05:18.717 --> 00:05:20.052
that's not supposed
to be on there.

